.TH PACTUI 1 "2026-07-08" "pacfz 1.0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pactui \- interactive terminal UI for exploring installed pacman
packages (experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pactui
[\-\-version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pactui
is a third front\-end sharing the exact same query engine and cache as
.BR pacfz (1)
and
.BR pacq (1),
built with the Textual framework. Unlike
.BR pacfz (1),
it does not use
.BR fzf (1)
and is not driven by command\-line flags; instead it presents a
full\-screen, mouse\-and\-keyboard\-driven interface with two screens.
.PP
This front\-end is
.B experimental
and does not yet have feature parity with
.BR pacfz (1)
/
.BR pacq (1).
Expect rough edges.
.PP
.B pactui
requires
.I python\-textual
to be installed; this is an optional dependency of the
.I pacfz
package, not a hard requirement.
.SH SCREENS
.SS Overview
The default screen on launch. Split into two panes:
.TP
.B Stats
A fixed\-shape summary tree: total packages installed, split into
official and foreign counts, and total installed size.
.TP
.B Log
A view of
.IR /var/log/pacman.log ,
parsed into individual install / upgrade / removal / command events
and listed most recent first.
.SS Search
A filter\-and\-preview screen: a search box and results table on the
left, a full colorized metadata preview of the highlighted package on
the right, and a panel of facet filters (foreign, orphan, dependency
status, notes, field search) along the bottom, similarly to
.BR pacfz (1)'s
own filter flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed pacfz version and exit, without launching the
interface.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
These apply throughout the interface unless noted otherwise.
.TP
.B f1
Switch to the Overview screen.
.TP
.B f2
Switch to the Search screen.
.TP
.B /
Focus the search box (Search screen only).
.TP
.BR j / k
Move the highlighted row down or up, in whichever table currently has
focus.
.TP
.B g
Jump to the top of the current table.
.TP
.B G
Jump to the bottom of the current table.
.TP
.B ctrl+r
Rebuild the package cache in the background and refresh the visible
results (Search screen only).
.TP
.B r
Refresh the Overview screen's stats and log without rebuilding the
package cache itself.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.PP
Every action is also reachable with the mouse: click a screen's tab
indicator to switch to it, click a table row to select it, click a
filter control to toggle it.
.SH STATE ACROSS SCREENS
Switching screens does not reset either one: the Search screen keeps
whatever search text, filters, and selected row you left it with, and
the Overview screen keeps its own state independently. Each screen's
filters are also independent of each other; there is a single shared
query engine underneath, but no shared filter state between screens.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, either via
.B q
or
.BR \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
.I python\-textual
is not installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PACFZ_DB_PATH
Overrides the package cache DB path outright. Default:
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/pacman_packages.db .
.TP
.B PACFZ_NOTES_DB_PATH
Overrides the notes DB path outright. Default:
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/pacfz/user_data.db .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pacman_packages.db
The package metadata cache, shared with
.BR pacfz (1)
and
.BR pacq (1).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pacfz/user_data.db
Per\-package user notes, shared with the other two front\-ends.
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
Read (not written) by the Overview screen's Log pane.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacfz (1),
.BR pacq (1),
.BR pacman (8)
.SH AUTHOR
marco-l
